  "summary": "Covariate and medication adjustments in GWAS and trio analyses are being corrected at the phenotype, liability, and summary-statistic levels.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is correction of inference bias arising from covariate and confounder handling in genomic association analyses. A Gaussian liability-model conversion from log odds is derived to correct collider bias in covariate-adjusted binary GWAS (pgen.1012348), and GEMRA adjusts phenotypes for medication use, with simulations reporting less bias and higher power than common approaches (pgen.1012366). MRGN addresses high-dimensional confounding in causal network inference from genomic trios (bib.bbag611), while KDRD estimates replicability of significant associations from a single study's summary statistics, tested on UK Biobank (preprint). The new elements are phenotype-level and summary-statistic-level corrections applied within association workflows, alongside a causal-inference method for confounded trio data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
